  "live_records": {
    "q-35294": {
      "dom_id": "step-q35294",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14221745/assets/b75586450ddee4f682f02539e02462d0aa5f88830b2989cc7cc2f4f6df635ade.png)\n\nFind ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(5+7x)^{3}(f(x)-x)^{4}$ for the function $f(x)$ plotted above.",
      "worked_solution": "From the graph, we get that ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)=0.$ \n\nFrom the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(5+7x)^{3}(f(x)-x)^{4}={lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(5+7x)^{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(f(x)-x)^{4}.\n$$\n\nWe calculate the limits of each factor, separately.\n\nApplying the power rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(5+7x)^{3} & ={({lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(5+7x))}^{3} \\\\  & =(5+7\\cdot (-1))^{3} \\\\  & =(-2)^{3} \\\\  & =-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(f(x)-x)^{4} & ={({lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(f(x)-x))}^{4} \\\\  & =(0-(-1))^{4} \\\\  & ={1}^{4} \\\\  & =1\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(5+7x)^{3}(f(x)-x)^{4} & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(5+7x)^{3}\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}(f(x)-x)^{4} \\\\  & =(-8)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =-8\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
